  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Beleaguered Castle. Type: Open Packer Solitaire. Rules: Build foundations UP by suit. Build tableau DOWN any suit. Empty spaces fill with any card.',
    Player: 'The 2 of Spades is buried under a King. You need to move that King, but the only empty space is on the other side of the board. Can you shift the sequence of Diamonds to free up a slot?',
    objective: 'Build all four Foundation piles up from Ace to King in the same suit.',
    gameplay: '1. **Foundations**: Build UP by suit (e.g., 2♥ on A♥). 2. **Wings (Tableau)**: The top (exposed) card of any Wing is available for play. You can build DOWN on the wings regardless of suit (e.g., playing a 6♠ on a 7♦). 3. **Moving Cards**: Only one card can be moved at a time. 4. **Empty Spaces**: If a Wing becomes empty, you can fill the space with ANY available card (usually a King is best to start a new sequence).',
    keyRules: [
      'Any suit can be built on any suit in the tableau (unlike Solitaire/Klondike where it must be alternating colors).',
      'Only the top card is movable.',
      'Empty spaces are critical—creating one is usually the primary Short-Term Goal.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'One player (solitaire). The player acts alone: they remove the four Aces to form the foundations, deal the remaining 48 cards into eight wings, then move exposed cards between the tableau and foundations until all cards are built up or no legal moves remain.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck.',
      equipment: 'Standard pack.',
      dealing: '1. Remove the 4 Aces and place them in a vertical column in the center (The Foundations). 2. Deal the remaining 48 cards face up into 8 horizontal rows (Wings) on either side of the Aces (4 rows left, 4 rows right). Each row has 6 cards overlapping so only the end card is accessible.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. **Foundations**: Build UP by suit (e.g., 2♥ on A♥). 2. **Wings (Tableau)**: The top (exposed) card of any Wing is available for play. You can build DOWN on the wings regardless of suit (e.g., playing a 6♠ on a 7♦). 3. **Moving Cards**: Only one card can be moved at a time. 4. **Empty Spaces**: If a Wing becomes empty, you can fill the space with ANY available card (usually a King is best to start a new sequence).',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Beleaguered Castle is a solitaire patience game and does not utilize a wagering or ante system.',
      deal: 'The initial setup of wings and foundations is performed automatically by the system dealer.',
      reveal_market: 'This is an open-information solitaire game where all cards are already visible on the tableau wings.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap cards from any external market; only tableau movements are allowed.',
      buy_stock: 'There is no remaining stock or boneyard in this game after the initial distribution of the wings.',
      fold: 'Solitaire games are played to completion or until no further moves are possible; folding is not applicable.',
      check: 'The game does not include a betting or vying structure where a check action would be appropriate.',
      call: 'There is no bet to match in solitaire; competition is based strictly on unblocking the deck.',
      bet: 'Success is measured by the number of cards moved to foundations rather than through financial betting.',
      raise: 'The complexity of the game is fixed by the deal; there are no wagering rounds to increase stakes.',
      declare: 'Winning combinations are verified by the foundation state rather than a separate declaration phase.',
      reveal_hand: 'There is no private hand in this open solitaire game; every card is visible on the board.',
      award_pot: 'The goal is a solved layout rather than the distribution of assets from a central pot.',
      play_card: 'Must follow descending tableau rules or ascending foundation rules.',
      draw: 'Every card is distributed to the wings at the start; no drawing occurs during the play phase.',
      discard: 'Cards are moved between piles rather than being removed from play into a discard pile.',
      pass: 'In solitaire, the player must either make a move or concede the deal; passing is not a valid action.',
      bid: 'Beleaguered Castle does not utilize a bidding system to determine game state or objectives.',
      meld: 'This is a packing solitaire game based on sequence building rather than forming melds.',
      go_out: 'The game concludes automatically when all cards reach the foundations or no moves remain.',
    },
